Probe and link EGL only when a GL API is enabled.

WHY: CheckWayland asks pkg-config for wayland-client, wayland-egl,
wayland-cursor, egl and xkbcommon as ONE group (sdlchecks.cmake:661),
and with SDL_WAYLAND_SHARED off it puts the whole group on the link
(line 723: list(APPEND EXTRA_LIBS ${PKG_WAYLAND_LIBRARIES})). With
SDL_OPENGL and SDL_OPENGLES both off, no EGL symbol is referenced
anywhere in src/video/wayland -- SDL_waylandopengles.c is under
SDL_VIDEO_OPENGL_EGL, and the three wl_egl_window_* calls that ARE
unconditional (SDL_waylandwindow.c:176, 2055, 2302) come from
wayland-egl, which is libwayland's, not mesa's. So -lEGL is a dead flag
-- and a fatal one for a --static consumer, because mesa builds no
libEGL.a and ld refuses a static link with a library it cannot find.

WHY THIS AND NOT dlopen: the alternative, SDL_WAYLAND_SHARED=ON, has
been measured on the image it was built for (bare metal, 2026-08-25):
static glibc's dlopen loads a second libc for the shared library, and
across that seam libasound segfaulted at its first call and
libwayland-client went silent after its first roundtrip -- a window
that acked its configure and never attached a buffer. Linking the
backends statically removes the seam. Read from the pinned tarball
(sha256 5f5993c5...), one hunk, generated with diff -u, applied with
the same `patch -p1 -N` the driver uses.

WHAT CHANGES: with GL off, egl leaves the probe list and therefore the
link; mesa leaves the recipe's build dependencies. With GL on, nothing
changes.

--- a/cmake/sdlchecks.cmake
+++ b/cmake/sdlchecks.cmake
@@ -658,7 +658,11 @@
 macro(CheckWayland)
   if(SDL_WAYLAND)
     set(WAYLAND_FOUND FALSE)
-    pkg_check_modules(PKG_WAYLAND "wayland-client>=1.18" wayland-egl wayland-cursor egl "xkbcommon>=0.5.0")
+    set(_veron_wayland_modules "wayland-client>=1.18" wayland-egl wayland-cursor "xkbcommon>=0.5.0")
+    if(SDL_OPENGL OR SDL_OPENGLES)
+      list(APPEND _veron_wayland_modules egl)
+    endif()
+    pkg_check_modules(PKG_WAYLAND ${_veron_wayland_modules})
 
     if(PKG_WAYLAND_FOUND)
       set(WAYLAND_FOUND TRUE)
